erican R&B/Soul singer, songwriter and actress born in Dallas, Texas on February 26, 1971.\r\nShe is known as the first lady of Neo-Soul. She also DJs under the name \"Lo Down Loretta Brown\".\r\nBefore devoting herself to singing, she used to rap under the \"Apples\" alias, and was also a member of the hip-hop group [a=Def-Ones] (Dallas, 1980s).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:10995","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":654334,"name":"Erica Wright"},{"id":1327944,"name":"Ebi Breezy"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Badu","Badu Erykah","DJ Badu","E .Badu","E,. Badu","E. Badu","E. Badu (Thanks to Waldo)","E.B","E.B.","E.Badu","E.badu","EB","Edykah Badu","Erekah Badu","Erica B","Erica B.","Erica Badu","Ericka Badu","Erika Bada","Erika Badu","Erikah Badu","Eriykah Badu","Eruka Badu","Eryakah Badu","Eryca Badu","Eryka Badu","Erykah","Erykah Badhu","Erykah Budu","Erykay Badu","e. Badu","e. badu","e.badu","eryKahBadu","エリカ・バドゥ","艾莉卡芭朵"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/10995-Erykah-Badu","type":"artist","urls":["https://erykahbadu.com/","https://www.instagram.com/erykahbadu/","https://www.mixcloud.com/erykah-she-ill-badu/","https://soundcloud.com/erykah-she-ill-badu","https://x.com/fatbellybella","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erykah_Badu","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCDOZs-fcPo0ab9mqUnyN4cw"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/13957210/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"13957210","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Project by [a=Maara (2)] (aka Maara-Louisa Dunbar) & [a=Roza Terenzi] (aka Katie Campbell).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:13957210","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":6802483,"name":"Katie Campbell (4)"},{"active":true,"id":9892309,"name":"Maara-Louisa Dunbar"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/13957210-Bass-Butches","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1622339/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1622339","image":"https://i.discogs.com/myOxPADf3PaC_WH4mRy6scaIlArFDyA4_ozMIvDpdgE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:525/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE2MjIz/MzktMTcxNzc2MzIy/MS01NDk2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/GrEYn9IdkIHKg0RXW6koSOOkKBcONXlAZgj5LFP1mrU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE2MjIz/MzktMTcxNzc2MzIy/MS01NDk2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"British DJ (born 1987 in Doncaster) and producer based in Berlin, Germany\r\n-------\r\nThrough both time in the studio and time on the road, Jamie Roberts has dedicated the last decade to developing his alias, Blawan – and in the process, he’s created a universe within techno that’s all his own. Roberts grew up in Barnsley, UK and from an early age was etching out his musical path as a drummer – a relic of the past which should come as no surprise to anyone familiar with his productions. Indeed, his discography as Blawan illuminates a natural fluency for rhythm, whether straight, stridently syncopated, or swinging somewhere in between.\r\n\r\nHis other aliases, Kilner and Bored Young Adults, like his collaborations with Pariah as Karenn and with Surgeon as Trade, have provided additional bandwidth for experimentation. Having released across the board of rippling jet-black minimalism, jubilant two-step vocal cuts, and savant grooving techno, the labels Roberts has worked with are appropriately varied: Hessle Audio, R&S, Clone’s Basement Series, Hinge Finger, and Black Sun as Blawan, plus The Trilogy Tapes and Avian under his other solo names. \r\n\r\nRoberts’ own label, TERNESC, was established in 2015 and has served as the home for his last five releases as Blawan. Having made the move to Berlin in 2015, his analogue-driven studio production and formidable live sets have propelled Roberts into exciting new directions, even as he maintains expert command of more traditional dance floor environments from behind the decks. His latest offering, the full-length Wet Will Always Dry, dropped in June 2018. It’s a breakthrough moment in Roberts’ discipline of auditory alchemy, and a tour-de-force of ambitious, nuanced techno for fans following his ever-explorative career.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1622339","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":2154017,"name":"Jamie Roberts"},{"id":5162776,"name":"Bored Young Adults"},{"id":5397764,"name":"Kilner"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["ブラ��ン"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1622339-Blawan","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/pages/Blawan/115678128712","https://soundcloud.com/ternesc","http://www.twitter.com/blawan","https://blawan.bandcamp.com","https://thequietus.com/interviews/blawan-jamie-roberts-interview/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1935123/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1935123","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Ekb8ed9KRqGwF79NL0TNVYWZVWaKhSJ98TTSIw64Zio/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:337/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5MzUx/MjMtMTQwOTE1MjY5/MC00NTQ0LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/w6gpL_H-zHEmEjQWC_-Ungc81ZghsqcDCavUkBjNI7U/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5MzUx/MjMtMTQwOTE1MjY5/MC00NTQ0LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Hip-hop collective from Seattle, Washington, led by Ishmael Butler (formerly [a=Digable Planets]).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1935123","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":273609,"name":"Ishmael Butler"},{"active":false,"id":3878230,"name":"Tendai Maraire"}],"namevariations":["Dal","Shabbaz Palaces"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1935123-Shabazz-Palaces","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.shabazzpalaces.com/","http://www.facebook.com/pages/Shabazz-Palaces/117954334892194","http://twitter.com/shabazzpalaces","http://instagram.com/shabazzpalaces","http://myspace.com/shabazzpalacesmusic","http://www.subpop.com/artists/shabazz_palaces","http://www.songkick.com/artists/2981826-shabazz-palaces","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shabazz_Palaces","http://genius.com/artists/Shabazz-palaces","http://www.whosampled.com/Shabazz-Palaces/","http://shabazzpalaces.bandcamp.com/","http://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLE1B75EF703D98B32"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1948644/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1948644","image":"https://i.discogs.com/WjrvcR8VQPmgnbA1W09yF4rGd3IKQNWZC3AtKWxb59o/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5NDg2/NDQtMTY1OTAwODkx/My02MTM3LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/sNzQR7rgRwt0XRhc9BnJT6uJ00cAtjbIB69MQwyhm9c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5NDg2/NDQtMTY1OTAwODkx/My02MTM3LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Old School Nerdcore / UK Hardcore Producer.\r\n[l=GAO] Owner.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1948644","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Ninja Remixing Team Totsumal","totsumal","突丸企画"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1948644-Totsumal","type":"artist","urls":["http://soundcloud.com/totsumal","https://twitter.com/totsumal"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/37913/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"37913","image":"https://i.discogs.com/X9q8iVYQ5nHKMInHnJvBdYq7cQOFeUh3Y8WbzLJOZaE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:522/w:387/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3OTEz/LTEzODQ5NjI0Mzct/NzYyMi5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/trxNSUY3YtbvXMAag0J7CPK4FIFpVmbF1Q3yijOtHHQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM3OTEz/LTEzODQ5NjI0Mzct/NzYyMi5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Michael Tyler (born September 22, 1970), better known by his stage name Mystikal, is an American rapper, and actor from New Orleans. A Persian Gulf war veteran who rose to stardom as a protégé of the rap impresario Master P, Tyler combined powerful, passionate vocals that would range from a conspiratorial whisper to vein-popping screams in the course of a few words, and was constantly accelerating and decelerating his delivery. The sound was new, but not unprecedented, as Tyler's vocals were reminiscent of R&B screamers like Little Richard and James Brown, using piano and saxophone sounds to accentuate the delivery.\r\n\r\nMystikal's debut album, Mystikal, was released on New Orleans-based independent record label Big Boy Records in 1994. He found himself in conflict with fellow New Orleans rappers signed to Cash Money Records including U.N.L.V., Lil Wayne and B.G.. They dissed him on tracks like \"Drag 'Em in Tha River\" by U.N.L.V. and \"Fuck Big Boy\" by The B.G.'z. He struck back with the diss \"Beware\" which was on his sophomore effort Mind of Mystikal. Mystikal's sister, [a=Michelle Tyler] (whom he had close ties with), sang the chorus on \"Not That Nigga\" and her fate became a major influence on Mystikal's music after her untimely death. The songs \"Dedicated To Michelle Tyler\", \"Murderer\" (both on Mind of Mystikal), \"Murder 2\", \"Shine\" (both on Unpredictable) and \"Murder III\" (on Let's Get Ready) refer to her murder.\r\n\r\nMystikal signed to Jive Records and released \"Mind of Mystikal\" in 1995. He signed to Master P's No Limit Records in 1997 alongside a slew of other New Orleans artists (adding the No Limit contract to his existing Jive deal) and released \"Unpredictable\" later that year. He appeared on most of the No Limit albums recorded from 1997-2000. In 1998, he released \"Ghetto Fabulous\". In 1999, he was going to release another album for No Limit titled \"Let's Get Ready To Rumble\". However this project, although recorded, kept being pushed back deeper into the year 2000 and by that time Mystikal had released himself from No Limit and released his recorded album \"Let's Get Ready To Rumble\" as the more simple titled \"Let's Get Ready\". In 2001, Mystikal released his final album for Jive entitled \"Tarantula\". His recording career lasted for another two years, until he was entangled in a sexual battery and extortion felony involving reportedly accusing his hairstylist of stealing $80,000 worth of his checks & using this as his justification to force her to perform oral sex on himself and two of his bodyguards (else he would report her supposed stealing to the police, but she ended up reporting the rape in turn). Mystikal was in prison from January 2004 until January 2010. He began to record new music after his release by creating a deal with Cash Money Records and doing independent collaborations. Mystikal found himself in jail again from late 2017 to early 2019 on reported rape charges that were dismissed due to apparent lack of evidence. On 1 August 2022, Mystikal was again arrested in Louisiana on charges relating to allegedly getting into a bout with a romantic partner - damaging house property, attacking & strangling her, raping her, and false imprisonment.\r\n\r\nWhen a free man, he has been doing live shows solo & with No Limit.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:37913","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":671950,"name":"Michael Tyler (2)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Mistical","Mistikal","Mistykal","Mr. Kal","Mystic","Mystical","Mystickal"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/37913-Mystikal","type":"artist","urls":["http://digitallibrary.tulane.edu/islandora/object/tulane%3A28455","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystikal"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4895415/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4895415","image":"https://i.discogs.com/xqmfLLlcuIerL1HqKpdZno3IhKheMYwCSaF--jG7kW4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:400/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4OTU0/MTUtMTc0NzU1MTY4/OS01MDMyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/t4Lq9qs5POuigt62fRNAm_VvQ5zbxyJkP40qmEjl0wc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ4OTU0/MTUtMTc0NzU1MTY4/OS01MDMyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Born in Washington D.C., Waleed moved to Europe to explore electronic music at night, whilst writing code by day. Immersing himself in the London and Berlin music scenes, his own production was heavily influenced by what he found there. In August 2021, Waleed quietly released his debut single ‘Se Rompen’. The response was anything but, with the track quickly receiving support from the likes of Ben-UFO, Floating Points and Four Tet.\r\n\r\nWaleed’s sound is at once ecstatic and melancholic with abrupt drops; engineering an unexpected narrative for the listener. With influences ranging from UK House to sounds from Waleed’s own Puerto Rican-Iraqi heritage, his tracks are a layered tapestry of sounds and styles. Signing to City Slang in 2022 Waleed is staking his claim as a producer who is undoubtedly one to watch.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4895415","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Waleed El Jawhary"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4895415-Waleed","type":"artist","urls":["https://waleedmusic.bandcamp.com/music"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/759/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"759","image":"https://i.discogs.com/U-RtvXhOB9mitoliWU-R4-8x9jD3DnlnqBs1BM-MRro/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:220/w:220/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc1OS0x/MzIxNjM3MDIyLmpw/ZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/qoLmHO3EiiepOPbmwUHXtHNir0baecJ-YM4eqxa8guw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTc1OS0x/MzIxNjM3MDIyLmpw/ZWc.jpeg","profile":"The longest serving artist on the Warp Records roster. Originally founded in 1988 by George \"DJ E.A.S.E.\" Evelyn and Kevin \"Boywonder\" Harper. Harper left before the release of Smokers Delight. When playing live they were also joined by MC Toz 180 and guitarist Chris Dawkins.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:759","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":31653,"name":"Robin Taylor-Firth"},{"active":false,"id":427445,"name":"Kevin Harper"},{"active":true,"i